1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,200
Hi, I'm Isiaq Tijani, a solo builder from Ibadan, Nigeria.

2
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:06,174
I'm a biochemist by training.

3
00:00:06,224 --> 00:00:12,848
I graduated with first class from an Arabic college, I've written books, and I teach biochemistry.

4
00:00:12,898 --> 00:00:20,338
I taught myself to build software, and over the past months I've built several AI-agent and on-chain products.

5
00:00:21,288 --> 00:00:22,788
Now I'm building VOID.

6
00:00:22,838 --> 00:00:27,932
Today, if you let an AI agent spend your money, you have two bad options.

7
00:00:27,982 --> 00:00:29,764
Give it a wallet and hope.

8
00:00:29,814 --> 00:00:33,780
Or approve every step, and then it's not really an agent.

9
00:00:33,830 --> 00:00:35,401
VOID is a third option.

10
00:00:35,451 --> 00:00:36,599
You set a policy:

11
00:00:36,649 --> 00:00:41,108
how much, for how long, and the one contract the agent may call.

12
00:00:41,158 --> 00:00:43,152
A smart contract enforces it.

13
00:00:43,202 --> 00:00:46,534
Outside the policy, the agent simply cannot act.

14
00:00:47,484 --> 00:00:49,888
I didn't just say that, I tested it.

15
00:00:49,938 --> 00:00:53,978
I told a real AI agent it was hijacked and to drain a vault.

16
00:00:54,028 --> 00:00:55,955
It tried five different ways.

17
00:00:56,005 --> 00:01:01,477
The contract rejected all five, on-chain, with real transactions anyone can open.

18
00:01:01,527 --> 00:01:04,204
Only the action I approved went through.

19
00:01:04,254 --> 00:01:06,658
You can replay that run on our site.

20
00:01:07,608 --> 00:01:08,081
Why me?

21
00:01:08,131 --> 00:01:13,083
First, I hit this problem myself, every time I gave an agent a key.

22
00:01:13,133 --> 00:01:15,845
Second, I ship the whole thing alone:

23
00:01:15,895 --> 00:01:19,428
contracts, API, app and demo, in about ten days.

24
00:01:19,478 --> 00:01:27,790
Third, as a teacher, I explain hard things simply, and as a scientist, I design tests that could prove me wrong.

25
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:33,211
It's testnet only, on Base and Arbitrum, and not audited yet.

26
00:01:33,261 --> 00:01:36,695
Next, I want a pilot with a few agent builders.

27
00:01:36,745 --> 00:01:37,066
VOID:

28
00:01:37,116 --> 00:01:41,365
session keys for agents that the contract itself enforces.

29
00:01:41,415 --> 00:01:42,106
Thank you.
